Hello!

I have an MSI MS-7350 motherborad with an onboard Realtek ALC888 HDA
codec. I need to specify
	 model=6stack-dig
to get the internal CD connector to show up, else automatic BIOS
scanning doesn't find it. Might be that you want to add the appropriate
DMI/PCI quirk stuff, so other users get the benefit of automatic
detection.

$ lspci -s 0:10.1
00:10.1 Audio device: nVidia Corporation MCP51 High Definition Audio (rev a2)
$ lspci -s 0:10.1 -n -vvv
00:10.1 0403: 10de:026c (rev a2)
        Subsystem: 1462:7350
        Control: I/O- Mem+ BusMaster+ SpecCycle- MemWINV- VGASnoop- ParErr- Stepping- SERR- FastB2B- DisINTx-
        Status: Cap+ 66MHz+ UDF- FastB2B+ ParErr- DEVSEL=fast >TAbort- <TAbort- <MAbort- >SERR- <PERR- INTx-
        Latency: 0 (500ns min, 1250ns max)
        Interrupt: pin B routed to IRQ 22
        Region 0: Memory at f9ff8000 (32-bit, non-prefetchable) [size=16K]
        Capabilities: <access denied>
        Kernel driver in use: HDA Intel
        Kernel modules: snd-hda-intel

